PS5 Bluetooth driver on 7.3.1: btusb as in v1.8.9/v2.1.x

rmux's tree carries an early draft of the PS5 Pro patch and re-adds the IW620 scan quirks. This puts back the
btusb changes v2.1.x shipped, replayed onto plain 7.3.1:
- IW620 (1286:2059): without BROKEN_EXT_SCAN/BROKEN_EXT_CREATE_CONN, so it finds new devices again (v2.1.1)
- PS5 Pro (0e8d:3605, QuartConz, mfoster978 PR #30): HCI on interface 3, IF3 routing undone before setup and
  shutdown (setup re-runs at every power on), the first HCI Reset retried after a cold boot, ACL OUT 0x0d
- Slim (0e8d:3603, WizGery): ACL on the second bulk OUT endpoint, unchanged
rmux's Bluetooth core changes (L2CAP, hci_sync, HIDP) stay.
